From 9cc0dc30814e65c537ac0153e302a2c32a5d0ffe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:56:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] a11y(ui): label sidebar toggle and logout icon buttons in
 layout
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The sidebar collapse/expand toggle and the logout button in the user
footer contain only an SVG icon; their accessible name came solely from
the `title` attribute, which screen readers are inconsistent about
announcing. Without an `aria-label`, VoiceOver/NVDA announce them as
just "button".

Add `aria-label` to both (the toggle label flips with state so the user
knows whether clicking will expand or collapse). The other icon buttons
in the header (Ayuda, Buscar página, Buscar actualización, Acerca de,
Cambiar tema) already had aria-labels.
---
 src/routes/+layout.svelte | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/routes/+layout.svelte b/src/routes/+layout.svelte
index 227814b..458791a 100644
--- a/src/routes/+layout.svelte
+++ b/src/routes/+layout.svelte
@@ -437,6 +437,7 @@
 							onclick={handleLogout}
 							class="text-white/60 hover:text-white transition-colors p-1 rounded"
 							title="Cerrar sesión"
+							aria-label="Cerrar sesión"
 						>
 							<svg
 								xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
@@ -465,6 +466,7 @@
 					onclick={() => (sidebarOpen = !sidebarOpen)}
 					class="p-2 rounded-lg text-text-secondary hover:bg-alt-row hover:text-text-primary transition-colors"
 					title={sidebarOpen ? 'Contraer menú' : 'Expandir menú'}
+					aria-label={sidebarOpen ? 'Contraer menú lateral' : 'Expandir menú lateral'}
 				>
 					<svg
 						xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
-- 
2.47.3

